@@ -0,0 +1,12 @@
+## Context
+
+`OrderService.cancel` calls `coupons.giveBack(code, order.customer)`. `Coupons.giveBack(code, order)` only releases when the recorded user equals its second argument, and `place` records the order id via `use(code, id)`. The customer never matches an order id, so nothing is released.
+
+## Decisions
+
+- Pass `order.id` (the `id` argument) to `giveBack`. The registry's ownership check stays as is, so cancelling one order never frees a coupon held by another.
+- Shipping: `shippingCost` uses `goods >= 5000` and the goods amount is after every discount, before VAT. A real order of exactly 5000 cents ships free, so no code change. Add an order-level test pinning this. If support still sees it, the likely cause is an order whose goods were 4999 or less (e.g. a coupon reduced them), which is correct per the README; the order number is needed to confirm.
+
+## Risks
+
+- None for the one-line fix; the report on shipping remains unreproduced.
