+## Why
+
+Paolo placed an order with a single-use welcome code, cancelled it the same day, and the code was refused as already used on the corrected order. The README says cancelling gives the coupon back. Support also reported €4.90 charged on goods of exactly €50.00.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Cancelling an order gives back its single-use coupon so a new order can use it. The cancel path passes the customer to the coupon registry where the order id is expected, so the coupon is never released.
+- Free shipping from €50.00: the current code and the shipping spec already agree (goods of 5000 cents ship free), and an order of exactly €50.00 was checked and ships free. No behavior change is planned. A regression test at order level is added, and the report is flagged for follow-up (see design).
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+<!-- none -->
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+- `discounts`: a single-use coupon is available again once the order that used it is cancelled.
+
+## Impact
+
+- `src/orders.ts` (`cancel`), tests in `test/`.
